  - app/(store)/basket/**          # Basket UI - no changes
  - sanity/schemaTypes/            # Sanity schemas - no changes
  - store/store.ts                 # Zustand store - no changes
  - lib/stripe/                    # Existing Stripe client config - no changes
  - tailwind.config.ts             # Design tokens - no changes
  - All existing tests - no changes

## Allowed Write Scope
  - app/(store)/checkout/address/** # Address page implementation
  - app/(store)/checkout/payment/** # Payment page implementation
  - app/actions/checkout/**         # Server actions for checkout
  - app/api/webhook/route.ts         # Webhook handler
  - tests/e2e/checkout/**            # NEW: E2E tests for checkout flow
  - lib/stripe-promise.ts            # NEW: Module-scope stripe loader

## Anti-Patterns (REJECT if observed)
  - Creating PaymentIntent in useEffect
  - Mocking Stripe in tests
  - Creating PaymentIntent at basket click
  - Not using compensation pattern
  - Loading stripe inside component

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# PHASE 1: FLOW ANALYSIS (from flow per ux slice.md)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------

## Flow Chunk Mapping
  | Slice | State Machine ID | Files | Notes |
  |-------|------------------|-------|-------|
  | Basket | B-2 | app/(store)/basket/page.tsx | Checkout click generates idempotency key |
  | Address | C-1 | app/(store)/checkout/address/page.tsx | PaymentIntent created here |
  | Payment | C-2 | app/(store)/checkout/payment/page.tsx | Stripe Elements render |
  | Webhook | W-1 | app/api/webhook/route.ts | Order creation + stock finalization |

## Critical Implementation Points
  - Step 8: Reserve stock FIRST, then create PaymentIntent (compensation pattern)
  - Step 17: React 18 StrictMode fixes for Stripe Elements
  - Step 18: elements.submit() before confirmPayment
  - Step 19: redirect: 'if_required' to keep card payments in-app
  - Webhook: Authoritative order creation, no client-side order writes

